<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palazzo della Pilotta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Palazzo della Pilotta is a large palace complex in Parma, begun by the Farnese dukes around 1583 and never completed. It houses the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teatro-farnese">Teatro Farnese</a>, the National Gallery of Parma, the Palatine Library and the archaeological museum. It was severely damaged by Allied bombing in 1944.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palazzo-della-pilotta.jpg" alt="Palazzo della Pilotta" width="320" height="120" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parma,_palazzo_della_pilotta_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The wooden Teatro Farnese, built in 1618 inside the <b>Pilotta</b> palace, staged its first spectacle only in 1628 and was used for just a few court festivities before falling out of use.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-parma-and-piacenza">Duchy of Parma and Piacenza · At a glance</a></li></ul></section>
